------- FILE main.asm
------- FILE repeat.asm LEVEL 2 PASS 3
      0  4cb4					      include	"repeat.asm"
      1  4cb4							; Fat Chip 64 - REPEAT (v0.13): echoes of the notes you play
      2  4cb4							;
      3  4cb4							; Each key pressed (overlay or MIDI in) is played again REPEATS times, every
      4  4cb4							; REPEAT TIME, each one REPEAT LEVEL as loud as the one before (velocity:
      5  4cb4							; the Game Boy and MidiNES scale their level by it). The echoes play on one
      6  4cb4							; or two "echo voices" (Game Boy pulse 2 and NES pulse 2 first, then pulse
      7  4cb4							; 1s), taken out of the chord while REPEAT is on - from what's spare once
      8  4cb4							; the notes and Fat Bass have theirs (v0.21: Polyphony > Fat Bass >
      9  4cb4							; effects; with nothing spare the echoes wait). Each echo sounds for
     10  4cb4							; 3/4 of the time between echoes. The SID doesn't echo.
     11  4cb4							;
     12  4cb4							; REPEAT on / off: the sound's default, the menu's REPEAT (AS SOUND / ON /
     13  4cb4							; OFF; ON uses the ADVANCED SOUND values), or the REPEAT action held (SPACE
     14  4cb4							; or a keytar button).
     15  4cb4							; REPEAT TIME: 1/4, 1/8 dotted, 1/8, 1/8T, 1/16 of the tempo, or FREE
     16  4cb4							; 80-500 ms. REPEATS: 1-8. REPEAT LEVEL: FULL, 90, 80, 70, 60, 50 %.
